DESCRIPTION >
    Hot log events for interactive search. Written by the processing workers
    via the Tinybird Events API; queried by the query-coordinator for the
    hot (0-7 day) window. The `attributes` column stores the original
    unstructured fields as a JSON string so the schema stays stable.

SCHEMA >
    `event_id` String `json:$.event_id`,
    `timestamp` DateTime64(3) `json:$.timestamp`,
    `service` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.service`,
    `severity` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.severity`,
    `message` String `json:$.message`,
    `attributes` String `json:$.attributes`,
    `trace_id` String `json:$.trace_id`,
    `source` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.source`,
    `region` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.region`,
    `version` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.version`

ENGINE "MergeTree"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "service, severity, timestamp"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toYYYYMMDD(timestamp)"
ENGINE_TTL "timestamp + INTERVAL 30 DAY"
